SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around the Branch Tour
DESCRIPTION:Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff to explore the natural world on a local neighbourhood tour in the Danforth/Coxwell area. Learn how to recognize different species and acquire fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance. \nThe tour will start and end at the Danforth/Coxwell Library\, Main Floor\, and will be guided by the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff. There may be uneven\, unpaved surfaces along the route. Please dress and prepare accordingly for this outdoor program (e.g. gloves/mittens\, hats\, sunscreen\, water\, comfortable shoes). This program takes place rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement weather\, registrants will be notified of an alternative date. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver. \nRegister for the event online. For assistance\, visit the branch or call 416-393-7783.
URL:https://beachmetro.com/event/natureto-trees-around-the-branch-tour/
LOCATION:Danforth Coxwell Library\, 1675 Danforth Avenue\, Toronto\, M4C 5P2
ORGANIZER;CN="Danforth Coxwell Branch%2C Toronto Public Library":MAILTO:dastaff@tpl.ca
END:VEVENT
